{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/828791-publish-1e-setting-now-or-wait-for-2e","id":828791,"title":"Publish 1E setting now, or wait for 2E?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-12T08:10:12-08:00","id":828791,"title":"Publish 1E setting now, or wait for 2E?","content":"For the last few months, I've been working on turning the city of Detroit, Michigan into a playable setting, primarily geared towards changelings (but with plenty of hooks for other types of supernaturals), in the style of <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/World_of_Darkness:_Chicago\" target=\"_blank\"><i>World of Darkness: Chicago</i></a> or <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/defaultadf7.html\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Venice Unmasked</i></a>. The trouble is, I've been working on it for so long that Changeling 2E is soon to be released, and now I'm reluctant to publish what I've written so far, since it'll be out-of-date almost as soon as I get it out there.<br /> <br /> Should I go ahead and post what I've got, and worry about making the conversion to 2E later? Or would it be wiser to wait, and see if new mechanics in 2E would throw a monkey-wrench into my plans?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/856697-motor-city-breakdown-a-playable-changeling-setting-for-detroit-michigan\" target=\"_blank\">Motor City Breakdown</a>, <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/19D2lK7otRprpHsJz0aZF0WucpMtoEgGQ2ExZJ-ud0a4/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\">Devil's Night in the D</a>, <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1uFgCI8m4gJ5kg1DneG0Cgu18bmUpe4RxDNDfI824G6M/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\">The Magical History Tour</a><br /> Accuracy Consultant on <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/AshesOfTheMotorCity.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Ashes of the Motor City</a><br /> Editor, Compiler, and Senior Contributor to <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1OxlnZCafIZtgPMCfikl0DJvWAwZKJDLk6lxh9hFPB1g/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Seas</a><br /> <b>Current Project(s)</b>: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/15v9c9IWq_HOjZoYPWqceTxQ0-z1epdN4pt5F6nMUYpE/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\">We Have Fought the Long Defeat</a>, a Late Antiquity/Early Medieval Dark Era for <i>Genius: The Transgression</i>; <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/12IQd13VQ0kHFY19yUBBkqVA-cKT0gZlByOkgYRkb-Ss/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Just Before the Dawn</i></a><i>,</i> a 1970s PtH Dark Era","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6327-super_dave","name":"Super_Dave","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6327_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-12T08:50:54-08:00","id":828814,"title":"","content":"I would say publish now and then when 2e is out, publish a conversion guide.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-12T10:46:59-08:00","id":828859,"title":"","content":"I suppose that makes sense. It could be a while before Changeling 2E is released, and I still haven't familiarized myself with the God-Machine rules (my usual gaming group has gone through some big life-changes in the last few years), so in any case I'd have to catch up on new developments before making the switch. <br /> <br /> I've basically got enough material for a PDF already, but it still needs a few things before it's completely ready (inter-chapter short fiction, stats for the characters I've designed, and perhaps a starter adventure). And of course, some input from the community before I go ahead and commit everything to &quot;paper&quot;. But I've got an introduction to the setting, a timeline of the (former) freehold of Detroit, the current socio-political situation, places of interest, an overview of the suburbs, and a slew of NPC bios.<br /> <br /> In fact, I think my biggest hurdle might be how I'm going to decide what information to cut out. Killing your little darlings is always difficult, but I must remember that players are smart people, and fully capable of doing their own research if they want to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/856697-motor-city-breakdown-a-playable-changeling-setting-for-detroit-michigan\" target=\"_blank\">Motor City Breakdown</a>, <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/19D2lK7otRprpHsJz0aZF0WucpMtoEgGQ2ExZJ-ud0a4/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\">Devil's Night in the D</a>, <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1uFgCI8m4gJ5kg1DneG0Cgu18bmUpe4RxDNDfI824G6M/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\">The Magical History Tour</a><br /> Accuracy Consultant on <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/AshesOfTheMotorCity.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Ashes of the Motor City</a><br /> Editor, Compiler, and Senior Contributor to <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1OxlnZCafIZtgPMCfikl0DJvWAwZKJDLk6lxh9hFPB1g/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Seas</a><br /> <b>Current Project(s)</b>: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/15v9c9IWq_HOjZoYPWqceTxQ0-z1epdN4pt5F6nMUYpE/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\">We Have Fought the Long Defeat</a>, a Late Antiquity/Early Medieval Dark Era for <i>Genius: The Transgression</i>; <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/12IQd13VQ0kHFY19yUBBkqVA-cKT0gZlByOkgYRkb-Ss/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Just Before the Dawn</i></a><i>,</i> a 1970s PtH Dark Era","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6327-super_dave","name":"Super_Dave","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6327_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-12T11:13:51-08:00","id":828876,"title":"","content":"I have one major question on setting write-up - Are you going with Seasonal Courts of 1ED or made new ones, like <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/changeling-the-lost-second-edition-court-creation-and-toronto/\" target=\"_blank\">proposed in spoiler</a>?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T16:06:48-08:00","id":831335,"title":"","content":"I'm actually planning on the Seasonal Courts being effectively dead in Detroit, or so fractured and far-removed from their original concepts that they can hardly be called &quot;seasonal&quot; any longer. They don't share power, they don't trade rulership of the freehold (or what's left of it), and their areas of influence are territorial, not temporal (i.e., they control neighborhoods, not portions of the year).<br /> <br /> Players will have the option of getting in on the ground floor of (re)creating an entire freehold, more-or-less from scratch. They can choose to restore the Wheelhouse to its rightful position if they like, or they can break away from the mistakes of the past and forge an entirely new freehold and court-system based on whatever they choose (like Detroit's major industries, or the different parts of an automobile, or even musical genres associated with the Motor City). I feel that this ties nicely into the transition from 1E to 2E, allowing the players to support whichever system they find most appealing, and giving players an uncommon amount of input into how their chronicle will play out.<br /> <br /> Courts are important in many <i>Changeling </i>chronicles, but it's pretty rare that players get to actually choose how their court system will work, which courts will comprise it, and who those courts' respective leaders will be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/856697-motor-city-breakdown-a-playable-changeling-setting-for-detroit-michigan\" target=\"_blank\">Motor City Breakdown</a>, <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/19D2lK7otRprpHsJz0aZF0WucpMtoEgGQ2ExZJ-ud0a4/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\">Devil's Night in the D</a>, <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1uFgCI8m4gJ5kg1DneG0Cgu18bmUpe4RxDNDfI824G6M/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\">The Magical History Tour</a><br /> Accuracy Consultant on <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/AshesOfTheMotorCity.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Ashes of the Motor City</a><br /> Editor, Compiler, and Senior Contributor to <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1OxlnZCafIZtgPMCfikl0DJvWAwZKJDLk6lxh9hFPB1g/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Seas</a><br /> <b>Current Project(s)</b>: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/15v9c9IWq_HOjZoYPWqceTxQ0-z1epdN4pt5F6nMUYpE/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\">We Have Fought the Long Defeat</a>, a Late Antiquity/Early Medieval Dark Era for <i>Genius: The Transgression</i>; <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/12IQd13VQ0kHFY19yUBBkqVA-cKT0gZlByOkgYRkb-Ss/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Just Before the Dawn</i></a><i>,</i> a 1970s PtH Dark Era","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6327-super_dave","name":"Super_Dave","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6327_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T18:39:42-08:00","id":831408,"title":"","content":"Well, with the Court creation system in 2e it'll be much more common for players to make those kinds of decisions out of character, collaboratively with the storyteller. But doing that in character, as the central conflict of a setting? Yeah, that sounds awesome!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T08:47:58-08:00","id":831769,"title":"","content":"I agree that you should publish it as it is. Not everyone will convert to 2E, so they'll have something they can use directly, and converting shouldn't be too hard for those who want to. Do let us know where and when you put it up. I'd love to read it. =)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kismet's <a href=\"http://www.wod.kismetrose.com/\" target=\"_blank\">WOD</a> - <a href=\"http://www.dnd.kismetrose.com/\" target=\"_blank\">D&amp;D</a> - <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/BoundinDreams\" target=\"_blank\">C:tL</a> - <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/TheNamelessEmpire\" target=\"_blank\">M:tC</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/227-kismetrose","name":"KismetRose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar227_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-20T14:02:21-08:00","id":834027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/828791-publish-1e-setting-now-or-wait-for-2e?p=831408#post831408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, with the Court creation system in 2e it'll be much more common for players to make those kinds of decisions out of character, collaboratively with the storyteller. But doing that in character, as the central conflict of a setting? Yeah, that sounds awesome!</div> </div> </div> </div>Glad you like it! I thought that Detroit would be a good fit with the new edition, since 2E is supposed to focus more on recovery and healing from trauma, two things which are very important to Detroit right now. I really can't think of a city which is better-suited for telling stories about dealing, growing, and healing (or one that's better-suited for a World of Darkness chronicle).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KismetRose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/828791-publish-1e-setting-now-or-wait-for-2e?p=831769#post831769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree that you should publish it as it is. Not everyone will convert to 2E, so they'll have something they can use directly, and converting shouldn't be too hard for those who want to. Do let us know where and when you put it up. I'd love to read it. =)</div> </div> </div> </div>Why, thank you! It's good to know that someone already likes the idea for my setting, and especially exciting that that person is the famed Kismet Rose (I'm a big fan of your website)! I'll do my best to live up to your expectations.<br /> <br /> As for where I'll be putting this thing: I plan to start a thread called <i>Motor City Breakdown</i> here on the forums, at least at first. Ultimately, once my fellow fans have helped me work out any kinks in the rules or twists-of-phrase that need fixing, I'd really like to convert the whole darn thing into a professional-looking PDF with those thorn-borders and so on, and give it away as a free download somewhere. I don't have any idea how I would go about converting it into a PDF, though (would I have to pay a graphic designer?), but I can cross that bridge when I come to it. For now, I'm focusing on not overloading the reader with details: I've learned a <i>lot</i> about Detroit, but not all of it is relevant to every player/Storyteller, and sometimes it's hard to distinguish &quot;unnecessary detail&quot; from &quot;local flavor&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/856697-motor-city-breakdown-a-playable-changeling-setting-for-detroit-michigan\" target=\"_blank\">Motor City Breakdown</a>, <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/19D2lK7otRprpHsJz0aZF0WucpMtoEgGQ2ExZJ-ud0a4/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\">Devil's Night in the D</a>, <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1uFgCI8m4gJ5kg1DneG0Cgu18bmUpe4RxDNDfI824G6M/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\">The Magical History Tour</a><br /> Accuracy Consultant on <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/AshesOfTheMotorCity.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Ashes of the Motor City</a><br /> Editor, Compiler, and Senior Contributor to <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1OxlnZCafIZtgPMCfikl0DJvWAwZKJDLk6lxh9hFPB1g/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Seas</a><br /> <b>Current Project(s)</b>: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/15v9c9IWq_HOjZoYPWqceTxQ0-z1epdN4pt5F6nMUYpE/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\">We Have Fought the Long Defeat</a>, a Late Antiquity/Early Medieval Dark Era for <i>Genius: The Transgression</i>; <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/12IQd13VQ0kHFY19yUBBkqVA-cKT0gZlByOkgYRkb-Ss/edit?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Just Before the Dawn</i></a><i>,</i> a 1970s PtH Dark Era","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6327-super_dave","name":"Super_Dave","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6327_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T14:13:30-08:00","id":839422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Super_Dave</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/828791-publish-1e-setting-now-or-wait-for-2e#post828791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the last few months, I've been working on turning the city of Detroit, Michigan into a playable setting, primarily geared towards changelings (but with plenty of hooks for other types of supernaturals), in the style of <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/World_of_Darkness:_Chicago\" target=\"_blank\"><i>World of Darkness: Chicago</i></a> or <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/defaultadf7.html\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Venice Unmasked</i></a>. The trouble is, I've been working on it for so long that Changeling 2E is soon to be released, and now I'm reluctant to publish what I've written so far, since it'll be out-of-date almost as soon as I get it out there.<br /> <br /> Should I go ahead and post what I've got, and worry about making the conversion to 2E later? Or would it be wiser to wait, and see if new mechanics in 2E would throw a monkey-wrench into my plans?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I feel you pain. I have a ebook for Manchester for Vampire, and that Changeling setting.... no way do I have time these days to update the NPCs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.darker-days.org\" target=\"_blank\">www.darker-days.org</a> - The Premier World of Darkness Podcast<br /> Co-designer and miniature painter for Noble Armada 3e<br /> Staff writer for CYBR Magazine <a href=\"https://shop.cybrmagazine.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://shop.cybrmagazine.com/</a><br /> Writer, developer, editor, layout for Darker Days Radio Publishing<br /> Writer for Cubicle 7 Wrath and Glory Revised","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/128-dr-ether","name":"Dr Ether","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar128_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"292"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T12:20:08-07:00","id":848328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Super_Dave</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/828791-publish-1e-setting-now-or-wait-for-2e?p=834027#post834027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why, thank you! It's good to know that someone already likes the idea for my setting, and especially exciting that that person is the famed Kismet Rose (I'm a big fan of your website)! I'll do my best to live up to your expectations.<br /> <br /> As for where I'll be putting this thing: I plan to start a thread called <i>Motor City Breakdown</i> here on the forums, at least at first. Ultimately, once my fellow fans have helped me work out any kinks in the rules or twists-of-phrase that need fixing, I'd really like to convert the whole darn thing into a professional-looking PDF with those thorn-borders and so on, and give it away as a free download somewhere. I don't have any idea how I would go about converting it into a PDF, though (would I have to pay a graphic designer?), but I can cross that bridge when I come to it. For now, I'm focusing on not overloading the reader with details: I've learned a <i>lot</i> about Detroit, but not all of it is relevant to every player/Storyteller, and sometimes it's hard to distinguish &quot;unnecessary detail&quot; from &quot;local flavor&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm so glad you've enjoyed the web site! I love seeing folks offering things for other Changeling players to use and be inspired by! <br /> <br /> I only know so much about more polished PDF design myself (and have been wanting to look into it further). You can always try asking around (Mr. Gone I'm sure is quite busy but is usually handy, awfully nice, and able to point folks in useful directions from <a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/</a>). If and when it gets into a condition that you want to post it, I would be honored to add it to Kismet's World of Darkness, with all due credit to you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kismet's <a href=\"http://www.wod.kismetrose.com/\" target=\"_blank\">WOD</a> - <a href=\"http://www.dnd.kismetrose.com/\" target=\"_blank\">D&amp;D</a> - <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/BoundinDreams\" target=\"_blank\">C:tL</a> - <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/TheNamelessEmpire\" target=\"_blank\">M:tC</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/227-kismetrose","name":"KismetRose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar227_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:"